    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">In humans, each cell contains 23 pairs of chromosomes. The 23rd pair are the <strong>sex chromosomes</strong>, which carry genes that determine an individual's biological sex. Females have two X chromosomes (<em>XX</em>), while males have one X chromosome and one Y chromosome (<em>XY</em>).</p>",
